    "english_commentary": [
      {
        "source": "valmikiramayan.net",
        "net_locator": "1-1-63, 1-1-64",
        "spans_beyond_this_verse": true,
        "text": "Vali had at one time killed Dundubhi and kicked his body over a long distance."
      },
      {
        "source": "valmikiramayan.net",
        "net_locator": "1-1-65",
        "spans_beyond_this_verse": true,
        "text": "Vali was able to throw that body, with whole of his foot, only up to two hundred bow-lengths, where the length of bow is said as six to seven feet. But Rama could kick that heap to ten yojana lengths, roughly ninety miles, only with a flip of his foot-toe's tip. But Sugreeva continued his grumbling, 'in those days this skeleton was with flesh and blood, now it became weight-less, thus show me more of your show of strength...' One Yojana is an ancient measure for distance, where that distance is covered in one yoking. Chambers dictionary puts it as five miles, and it is not agreeable for it was British-Indian revenue measure. Traditionally it is four krosha-s and thus each yojana is nine to ten miles."
      }
    ],
